{"id":"333e9485e0336b804533a12b","source":"rvvoenkor-tg","source_name":"Operation Z Russian Spring","platform":"telegram","url":"https://t.me/RVvoenkor/122502","published_at":"2026-09-03T01:23:01Z","collected_at":"2026-09-03T01:30:54.582190Z","title":"","text":"‼️ 🇷🇺 🇩🇪 Заявление Россотрудничества о закрытии Русского дома в Берлине \"Больше 40 лет Русский дом в Берлине является надёжным культурным мостом между двумя народами. Внутри него работает крупнейший в Западной Европе русский книжный магазин. ▪️ Последние 20 лет преподаватели русского со всей страны ежегодно собираются в Берлине на Неделю русского языка. ▪️ За последние 15 лет Русский дом посетило более 3 миллионов гостей (почти все население Берлина). ▪️ Несмотря на бессмысленное, вредное для наших народов и абсолютно беспрецедентное давление на Русский дом последние 4 года, каждое его мероприятие регулярно собирает в немецкой столице аудиторию в 500-700 человек. ▪️ Среди недавних масштабных событий: выставка современных российских художников, выступление хорового ансамбля Гнесинки, показ немцам более 100 новых российских фильмов. ▪️ Только в этом году более 600 человек занимались в русском языковом клубе. Работали мастерские, кружки, в том числе для детей. ▪️ Очевидно, что правительство Германии в очередной раз действует в ущерб интересам своего народа, пытаясь уничтожить многолетние международные культурные связи. В отношении Русского дома с февраля этого года по указанию немецки","html":"","media":[],"author":"Operation Z Russian Spring","language":"und","group":"ru-milbloggers","perspective":"russian","trust":"low","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"7ab69ff5cf0caab99330adaa1251fb583c96664a95ddb42f6cf4cb4cc633385e","original_text_chars":2119,"original_html_chars":7899,"text_truncated":true,"media_count":13,"platform":{"post":"RVvoenkor/122502"}}}
{"id":"dd5c1264cd51a94124f6e494","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/03/anthony-albanese-one-nation-jim-chalmers-labor-liberal-angus-taylor-tobacco-plan-ntwnfb","published_at":"2026-09-03T01:19:23Z","collected_at":"2026-09-03T01:31:12.531886Z","title":"Australia news live: Marles says US relationship ‘transcends governments of the day’; Sydney to get new ferry stop","text":"19.06 EDT Marles says US-Australia alliance as relevant as ever Richard Marles just spoke to the ABC from Washington DC, saying Australia’s alliance with the US remains as relevant today “as it ever has” in a “very challenging” environment. Marles has been meeting with his US counterpart, Pete Hegseth . He was asked if he believes president Donald Trump’s ongoing conflict with Iran and the US’s posturing towards other countries had affected Australian’s trust in the two country’s relationship. He said: Our alliance with the United States is something that’s been built over decades. It really does transcend governments of the day. Our collaboration as two defence forces is really central to providing deterrence and building peace and stability in the Indo-Pacific, which is ultimately what underwrites every Australians’ safety. The alliance is as relevant today in a very challenging and difficult world as it has ever been , and it’s profoundly important that we are making sure that it continues to evolve and to grow and to meet the circumstances of the moment. And that’s what we’re doing. The Australian deputy prime minister and minister of defence, Richard Marles, during a meeting w","html":"","media":["https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/2d5da6d125214232437324ff05baebf81065c9dd/0_0_6390_4567/master/6390.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none"],"author":"Nick Visser","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"16f67fd265457e178dcdc02292530f9df916bafb46a29d784d6d19ab0a75e6f6","original_text_chars":1313,"original_html_chars":3637,"text_truncated":true,"media_count":1,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/03/anthony-albanese-one-nation-jim-chalmers-labor-liberal-angus-taylor-tobacco-plan-ntwnfb","entry_link":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/03/anthony-albanese-one-nation-jim-chalmers-labor-liberal-angus-taylor-tobacco-plan-ntwnfb"}}}
{"id":"aed1d355d7d2cea359902c33","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/03/teenager-charged-after-near-complete-amputation-of-boys-hand-in-sydney-ntwnfb","published_at":"2026-09-03T00:24:33Z","collected_at":"2026-09-03T01:31:14.172864Z","title":"Boy charged after teenager's hand nearly cut off in Sydney","text":"NSW police arrested and charged a 15-year-old boy with wounding a person with intent to cause grievous bodily harm after a teen’s hand was nearly cut off. Photograph: Steven Saphore/AAP View image in fullscreen NSW police arrested and charged a 15-year-old boy with wounding a person with intent to cause grievous bodily harm after a teen’s hand was nearly cut off. Photograph: Steven Saphore/AAP Sydney Boy charged after ‘near-complete amputation’ of teenager’s hand in Sydney NSW police called to Redfern on Wednesday night found a 17-year-old with a partially severed hand Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates Get our breaking news email , free app or daily news podcast Guardian staff Wed 2 Sep 2026 20.24 EDT First published on Wed 2 Sep 2026 20.08 EDT Share Prefer the Guardian on Google A teenage boy will face court today after a “near-complete amputation” of a boy’s hand during an alleged assault in Sydney on Wednesday night. New South Wales police were called to Redfern about 6pm last night and found a 17-year-old with a partially severed hand. Police allege he was assaulted by another boy, aged 15, with a knife in a car park on Morehead Road. NSW paramedics attende","html":"","media":["https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/554d2a6beb218a5c025d3d1f3e9bcea631762520/282_0_2816_2253/master/2816.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none"],"author":"Guardian staff","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"c94b36a80af2877f87ff0e1df9a4e094b4b7ec268fb722a